   {
     "heading": "5. Public, social, and historical competitive data",
-    "body": "Some data is visible to other users when you use current public or social features. This may include nickname, coin-rank avatar, profile card settings and style, the short profile-card caption you write yourself (available with a Pro profile card), streak, rank, Peak floor, steps and weekly result, weekly coins earned (shown to members of your Peak room), historical Arena and tournament results from earlier app versions, premium markers, friend activity, activity likes, community pack author information, seller notifications, and similar profile fields. Your profile-card caption is visible to other players who open your profile card; other players can report it, and we may remove captions that break our rules. If you answer a poll in the App, we record only which questions your account has already answered, so that you cannot vote twice; the option you choose is added only to aggregated counts and is not stored with your account ID. Your own answers may be kept on your device. Other users only see aggregated results. When you save a video to your favorites, the App may show other users how many people saved that video; this is an aggregated count only and does not reveal who saved it. Visibility depends on the feature: some fields may be public to app users, some visible to friends, some visible to community pack buyers or sellers, and some visible only to moderators/admins.\n\nIf you have Phraseman Plus, other users may see a Plus marker (for example, a ring around your avatar) next to your nickname in friends lists, leaderboards, Peak rooms, and community features. The marker shows only that Plus is currently active; it does not show your plan, price, renewal date, how you got Plus, or any payment details.\n\nThe Peak groups players into weekly rooms of up to 30 places for each study language. Other app users who open the room can see your nickname, avatar and cosmetic style, your steps, place and weekly result. Some places in a room may be filled by computer-controlled participants rather than real people. Weekly room records are kept as part of the Peak history; your entry is removed from them when your account is deleted.\n\nWhen you use the Together feature with friends, those friends may see whether you studied today, which days of the current week you studied, how many days you both studied on the same day — including your shared streak in a row and its best length — the resulting friendship level and progress. Friends may also send or receive nudge signals through this feature.\n\nOnly friends you have accepted (not other users) may also see: in the weekly friend summary, how many study sessions you completed that week, your best day, and your Peak floor; in the shared phrase of the day, the phrase option you chose; in Learn Together and Duel, that you invited them and the result of a duel between the two of you; and, when you send a friend an energy gift, that it came from you.\n\nHistorical records created by retired features (such as the old Quiz mode, Arena matches and friend duels, tournaments, clubs, friend gifts, or the old ideas board (submitted ideas, likes and reports on ideas)), including old results or participation records, may be retained only as reasonably necessary for security, fraud or abuse prevention, dispute handling, legal compliance, backup expiry, or deletion integrity. Account deletion is designed to delete or de-identify those historical records controlled by Knowly, subject only to the limited retention grounds described in this Policy. Those historical records are not presented as currently available gameplay features."
+    "body": "Some data is visible to other users when you use current public or social features. This may include nickname, coin-rank avatar, profile card settings and style, the short profile-card caption you write yourself (available with the Pro profile card, a card style you can get with coins; it is not a subscription), streak, rank, Peak floor, steps and weekly result, weekly coins earned (shown to members of your Peak room), historical Arena and tournament results from earlier app versions, the Plus marker described below, friend activity, activity likes, community pack author information, seller notifications, and similar profile fields. Your profile-card caption is visible to other players who open your profile card; other players can report it, and we may remove captions that break our rules. If you answer a poll in the App, we record only which questions your account has already answered, so that you cannot vote twice; the option you choose is added only to aggregated counts and is not stored with your account ID. Your own answers may be kept on your device. Other users only see aggregated results. Visibility depends on the feature: some fields may be public to app users, some visible to friends, some visible to community pack buyers or sellers, and some visible only to moderators/admins.\n\nIf you have Phraseman Plus, other users may see a Plus marker (for example, a ring around your avatar) next to your nickname in friends lists, leaderboards, Peak rooms, and community features. The marker shows only that Plus is currently active; it does not show your plan, price, renewal date, how you got Plus, or any payment details.\n\nPeak groups players into weekly rooms of up to 30 places for each study language. Other app users who open the room can see your nickname, avatar and cosmetic style, your steps, place and weekly result. Some places in a room may be filled by computer-controlled participants rather than real people. Weekly room records are kept as part of the Peak history; your entry is removed from them when your account is deleted.\n\nWhen you study with friends in the Friends section, those friends may see whether you studied today, which days of the current week you studied, how many days you both studied on the same day, your current and longest shared streak, and the resulting friendship level and progress. Friends may also send or receive nudges through this feature.\n\nOnly friends you have accepted (not other users) may also see: in the weekly friend summary, how many study sessions you completed that week, your best day, and your Peak floor; in the shared phrase of the day, the phrase option you chose; in Learn together and duels, that you invited them and the result of a duel between the two of you; and, when you send a friend an energy gift, that it came from you.\n\nHistorical records created by retired features (such as the old Quiz mode, Arena matches, the old friend duels (not the current duels with friends described above), tournaments, clubs, the old friend gifts (not the current energy gift), or the old ideas board (submitted ideas, likes and reports on ideas)), including old results or participation records, may be retained only as reasonably necessary for security, fraud or abuse prevention, dispute handling, legal compliance, backup expiry, or deletion integrity. Account deletion is designed to delete or de-identify those historical records controlled by Knowly, subject only to the limited retention grounds described in this Policy. Those historical records are not presented as currently available gameplay features."
