of a pack (title, description, and card text) may be sent to our AI provider (OpenAI) for review and automatic translation. Translated versions may be shown to other users who view the pack. When we reply to a report you sent, a moderator may use AI assistance to draft the reply from the report text; a person reviews the reply before it is sent to you in the App.\n\nWhen a Community Pack is approved for publication, the text of its cards in the language being learned (up to 300 characters per card) may be sent from our servers to our AI provider (OpenAI) to generate spoken audio for the cards. Only the card text is sent; no account details, names, or identifiers are sent with it. The generated audio files are stored in our cloud storage (Google Firebase) and played to users who open the pack. Because a clip depends only on its text, the same clip may be reused for identical card text in other packs. Audio is kept for as long as it is needed to provide the packs that use it and may be removed at any time.\n\nWe may review, block, remove, hide, de-identify, retain, or disclose user content, comments, and reports when needed to operate moderation, enforce the Terms, protect users, investigate abuse, handle disputes, prevent fraud, comply with law, respond to copyright or rights complaints, or preserve service integrity."
