     "heading": "8. App messages, reactions, polls, and surveys",
-    "body": "The App may show in-app messages, polls, product questions, cancellation surveys, VIP surveys, or similar prompts. If you respond, react, vote, dismiss, claim a reward, or otherwise interact, we may process response content, selected options, reaction type, vote choice, message IDs, survey IDs, timestamps, eligibility state, reward state, user or stable app IDs, and related metadata.\n\nWe use this information to operate messages and polls, prevent duplicate rewards or abuse, understand product feedback, improve the App, maintain audit records, and apply entitlements or rewards where applicable."
+    "body": "The App may show in-app messages, polls, product questions, cancellation surveys, VIP surveys, or similar prompts. If you respond, react, vote, dismiss, claim a reward, or otherwise interact, we may process response content, selected options, reaction type, vote choice, message IDs, survey IDs, timestamps, eligibility state, reward state, user or stable app IDs, and related metadata. For polls, the option you choose is added only to aggregated counts and is not stored with your account; we keep only a record that your account has already answered (see section 5).\n\nWe use this information to operate messages and polls, prevent duplicate rewards or abuse, understand product feedback, improve the App, maintain audit records, and apply entitlements or rewards where applicable."
