, and you can withdraw that consent at any time in the App's privacy settings. If you do not opt in, or if you withdraw consent, these two features are not shown and the associated text is not sent to the AI provider; the rest of the lesson (including the correct answer) continues to work normally. From version 2.0.0, these features are not available and no mistake text is sent to the AI provider for them.\n\nAI dialogues (scenario practice conversations and the free-form companion chat) also require your explicit, separate opt-in before you can open them for the first time, and you can withdraw that consent at any time in the App's privacy settings. If you do not opt in, or if you withdraw consent, these screens do not open and your messages are not sent to the AI provider.\n\nAI dialogues keep a limited, structured memory so a conversation can continue between sessions: a short learning summary for each study language (for example topics you practised, recurring language mistakes, and phrases worth reviewing) and resume checkpoints for each scenario. Knowly does not retain the raw transcript of your dialogues for this memory. The memory is stored in your account, is used only to personalise your dialogues, is never shown to other users, and is deleted together with your account. A copy of these summaries may also be kept on your device so the screen opens instantly; that copy is removed when you sign out, switch accounts, or delete the memory. You can delete all saved memory for a study language at any time in the App. Please do not tell the AI sensitive personal data (health, finances, legal matters, identifiers or passwords).\n\nWhile an AI dialogue is in progress, we keep the messages of that conversation (your messages and the AI replies) on our servers so the conversation can continue and a repeated request is not processed twice. These session records are kept only as long as needed for that purpose and for security and abuse prevention.\n\nMessages in AI dialogues are checked automatically for safety, including by our AI provider's moderation service. If a message is flagged, we may keep that message and a short excerpt of the preceding conversation as a safety record that only authorised moderators can review. Safety records are kept only as long as needed for safety, abuse prevention, or legal reasons. If you ask the App to translate text in a dialogue, the text and its translation may be kept in a shared translation cache that is not linked to your account."
