When you buy a gift, we process your email address, the plan, the recipient name and sender name you enter for the certificate, and the delivery method you choose: a code sent to your email or a gift link that you share yourself. We also process order identifiers, payment status, amount, currency, the activation code or gift link, and payment-provider transaction references. The certificate, gift email, and gift page show the plan and the names you entered; anyone who opens the gift link can see them. A gift is activated when the recipient enters the code or opens the gift link in the App; we then link the gift to the recipient's account to turn on Plus, or to extend an active Plus period, and to prevent repeated use. An unused gift code or gift link expires 365 days after purchase. You can cancel a code or gift link until it is activated; after cancellation it stops working, and refunds for cancelled gifts are issued manually within 5 business days to the original payment method. We do not show the buyer the recipient's account, progress, or other personal data. Card and PayPal payment credentials are collected by Stripe or PayPal, not by Knowly."
