   {
     "heading": "14. Website, cookies, leads, and web purchases",
-    "body": "The Knowly website uses local storage and session storage for essential preferences and flows, including theme choice, quiz progress, first-touch UTM attribution, lead email, cached prices, and your Meta Pixel consent choice. It also sends limited website events (page category, visit/view, store clicks, and quiz/checkout funnel events) to our Cloud Function, which stores aggregate counters. To protect that endpoint from abuse, we create a short-lived hash of the visitor IP address for rate limiting; hosting providers may also process IP addresses and request logs.\n\nIf Meta Pixel is enabled, we load it only after opt-in consent in the EU, EEA, UK, and Switzerland. You can accept, reject, or later change that choice using the \"Cookie settings\" link in the website footer.\n\nIf you request a quiz plan by email, we process your email address, quiz answers, UTM attribution, page, consent choice, and delivery/unsubscribe status to send the requested plan. We send follow-up product emails only when you separately opt in; you can withdraw that consent through the unsubscribe link in any such email or by contacting us.\n\nIf you use the Knowly website contact form, email support, or legal request channels, we may process your name, email address, message, topic, page URL, user-agent, forwarded IP header, support metadata, account identifiers you provide, and our replies. To respond faster, support messages may be triaged and answered with AI assistance: the text of your message and related support context may be shared with our AI provider (OpenAI) to classify the request and draft a reply, and routine replies may be sent automatically. You can ask for human review in your reply at any time.\n\nFor website purchases, we process your email, selected plan, quiz/UTM attribution, order identifiers, payment status, amount, currency, activation code, and payment-provider transaction references.\n\nGifts of Phraseman Plus for another person are sold only on the website. When you buy a gift, we process your email address, the plan, the recipient name and sender name you enter for the certificate, and the delivery method you choose: a code sent to your email or a gift link that you share yourself. We also process order identifiers, payment status, amount, currency, the activation code or gift link, and payment-provider transaction references. The certificate, gift email, and gift page show the plan and the names you entered; anyone who opens the gift link can see them. A gift is activated when the recipient enters the code or opens the gift link in the App; we then link the gift to the recipient's account to turn on Plus, or to extend an active Plus period, and to prevent repeated use. You can cancel a code or gift link until it is activated; after cancellation it stops working, and refunds for cancelled gifts are handled manually through support. We do not show the buyer the recipient's account, progress, or other personal data. Card and PayPal payment credentials are collected by Stripe or PayPal, not by Knowly."
+    "body": "The Knowly website uses local storage and session storage for essential preferences and flows, including theme choice, quiz progress, first-touch UTM attribution, lead email, cached prices, and your Meta Pixel consent choice. It also sends limited website events (page category, visit/view, store clicks, and quiz/checkout funnel events) to our Cloud Function, which stores aggregate counters. To protect that endpoint from abuse, we create a short-lived hash of the visitor IP address for rate limiting; hosting providers may also process IP addresses and request logs.\n\nIf Meta Pixel is enabled, we load it only after opt-in consent in the EU, EEA, UK, and Switzerland. You can accept, reject, or later change that choice using the \"Cookie settings\" link in the website footer.\n\nIf you request a quiz plan by email, we process your email address, quiz answers, UTM attribution, page, consent choice, and delivery/unsubscribe status to send the requested plan. We send follow-up product emails only when you separately opt in; you can withdraw that consent through the unsubscribe link in any such email or by contacting us.\n\nIf you use the Knowly website contact form, email support, or legal request channels, we may process your name, email address, message, topic, page URL, user-agent, forwarded IP header, support metadata, account identifiers you provide, and our replies. To respond faster, support messages may be triaged and answered with AI assistance: the text of your message and related support context may be shared with our AI provider (OpenAI) to classify the request and draft a reply, and routine replies may be sent automatically. You can ask for human review in your reply at any time.\n\nFor website purchases, we process your email, selected plan, quiz/UTM attribution, order identifiers, payment status, amount, currency, activation code, and payment-provider transaction references.\n\nGifts of Phraseman Plus for another person are sold only on the website. When you buy a gift, we process your email address, the plan, the recipient name and sender name you enter for the certificate, and the delivery method you choose: a code sent to your email or a gift link that you share yourself. We also process order identifiers, payment status, amount, currency, the activation code or gift link, and payment-provider transaction references. The certificate, gift email, and gift page show the plan and the names you entered; anyone who opens the gift link can see them. A gift is activated when the recipient enters the code or opens the gift link in the App; we then link the gift to the recipient's account to turn on Plus, or to extend an active Plus period, and to prevent repeated use. An unused gift code or gift link expires 365 days after purchase. You can cancel a code or gift link until it is activated; after cancellation it stops working, and refunds for cancelled gifts are issued manually within 5 business days to the original payment method. We do not show the buyer the recipient's account, progress, or other personal data. Card and PayPal payment credentials are collected by Stripe or PayPal, not by Knowly."
