   {
     "heading": "19. Retention",
-    "body": "We retain information only as long as reasonably needed for the purposes described in this Policy, unless a longer period is required or permitted by law.\n\nTypical retention criteria:\n- Local app data remains on your device until you delete it, use account deletion, clear app data, uninstall, or reset relevant device storage; backup/keychain behavior may vary by platform\n- Active cloud progress, profile, entitlement, and feature data is retained while your account or app instance is active\n- Reports, moderation records, safety records, purchase records, entitlement records, referral records, reward records, surveys, AI quota/billing/safety logs, analytics/error records, and fraud-prevention records may be retained longer where needed for safety, disputes, legal compliance, chargebacks, refunds, accounting, moderation integrity, abuse prevention, cost control, or auditability\n- Website quiz leads and marketing-consent records are retained while needed to provide the requested plan, respect consent or unsubscribes, prevent abuse, and keep reasonable business/legal records\n- Website contact/support messages are retained as long as needed to respond and keep support/security/legal records\n- Website payment/order records are retained as needed for payment, tax, accounting, refunds, chargebacks, fraud prevention, and legal obligations; payment providers retain payment data under their own policies\n- An account signed in with Google or Apple that you asked us to delete is retained for a 14-day grace period before irreversible deletion, so that an accidental deletion can be undone; during that period the account cannot be used and the data is not processed for any other purpose. A guest account (used without signing in with Google or Apple) cannot be restored, so its server-side data is deleted as soon as the deletion request reaches our servers and they confirm that no Google or Apple sign-in is linked to it; if this cannot be confirmed at that moment, the ordinary 14-day period applies\n- A minimal deletion record (hashed account identifiers, date, reason) is retained to demonstrate completed deletion requests\n- Backups and logs may persist until overwritten or deleted under normal retention cycles\n- In-app error and app activity logs (the limited app health records described in section 10) are deleted automatically 90 days after they are created\n\nWe do not promise automatic deletion after a fixed inactivity period unless such a deletion job is implemented and active."
+    "body": "We retain information only as long as reasonably needed for the purposes described in this Policy, unless a longer period is required or permitted by law.\n\nTypical retention criteria:\n- Local app data remains on your device until you delete it, use account deletion, clear app data, uninstall, or reset relevant device storage; backup/keychain behaviour may vary by platform\n- Active cloud progress, profile, entitlement, and feature data is retained while your account or app instance is active\n- Reports, moderation records, safety records, purchase records, entitlement records, referral records, reward records, surveys, AI quota/billing/safety logs, analytics/error records, and fraud-prevention records may be retained longer where needed for safety, disputes, legal compliance, chargebacks, refunds, accounting, moderation integrity, abuse prevention, cost control, or auditability\n- Website quiz leads and marketing-consent records are retained while needed to provide the requested plan, respect consent or unsubscribes, prevent abuse, and keep reasonable business/legal records\n- Website contact/support messages are retained as long as needed to respond and keep support/security/legal records\n- Website payment/order records are retained as needed for payment, tax, accounting, refunds, chargebacks, fraud prevention, and legal obligations; payment providers retain payment data under their own policies\n- An account signed in with Google or Apple that you asked us to delete is retained for a 14-day grace period before irreversible deletion, so that an accidental deletion can be undone; during that period the account cannot be used and the data is not processed for any other purpose. A guest account (used without signing in with Google or Apple) cannot be restored, so its server-side data is deleted as soon as the deletion request reaches our servers and they confirm that no Google or Apple sign-in is linked to it; if this cannot be confirmed at that moment, the ordinary 14-day period applies\n- A minimal deletion record (hashed account identifiers, date, reason) is retained to demonstrate completed deletion requests\n- Backups and logs may persist until overwritten or deleted under normal retention cycles\n- In-app error and app activity logs (the limited app health records described in section 10) are deleted automatically 90 days after they are created\n\nWe do not promise automatic deletion after a fixed inactivity period unless such a deletion job is implemented and active."
